FADE IN:

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - NIGHT #1#

Rain hammers the glass. A lamp turns, slow and patient.

LISA (60s), weathered, wipes the lens with a cloth. She hums something *old*.

LISA
(to herself)
One more night. Just one more.

A KNOCK at the door below. Lisa freezes.

LISA (CONT'D)
Who's there?

TOM (O.S.)
It's Tom. From the harbour. Let me in, **please**.

[[Check whether Tom should already be wet here.]]

EXT. HARBOUR - CONTINUOUS

Waves break over the pier. TOM (40s) shields his face, a canvas bag over one shoulder.

TOM
The boat's gone. Jürgen took it out an hour ago.

CUT TO:

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - STAIRWELL - NIGHT

Lisa descends, lantern raised. The stairs spiral down into darkness.

LISA
You came all this way to tell me _that_?

TOM
I came because nobody else would.

BRICK
Screw retirement.

STEEL ^
Screw retirement.

/* An omitted beat about the radio that we cut in the second draft. */

> THE END <
